WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.612
- If you don't stand for something,

00:00:01.612 --> 00:00:02.445
in this industry,

00:00:02.445 --> 00:00:03.501
you will for everything

00:00:03.501 --> 00:00:05.372
and you will not be
compensated on the way down.

00:00:05.372 --> 00:00:09.054
And if you believe every
negative thing about you,

00:00:09.054 --> 00:00:10.134
you're not going to get out of bed.

00:00:10.134 --> 00:00:13.384
One bad thing does not define who I am.

00:00:14.505 --> 00:00:17.094
I am so much more than a failed TV show.

00:00:17.094 --> 00:00:19.133
- She began her career in the 1990's

00:00:19.133 --> 00:00:21.232
appearing on television sitcoms.

00:00:21.232 --> 00:00:24.823
Her breakthrough role was in a
teen comedy film Bring It On.

00:00:24.823 --> 00:00:26.391
She stars as the lead character

00:00:26.391 --> 00:00:29.017
in the drama series Being Mary Jane.

00:00:29.017 --> 00:00:30.159
She's Gabrielle Union

00:00:30.159 --> 00:00:32.893
and here's my take on her
Top 10 Rules of Success.

00:00:32.893 --> 00:00:34.658
Rule number one is my personal favorite

00:00:34.658 --> 00:00:36.853
and I'd love to know which
one you guys like the best.

00:00:36.853 --> 00:00:38.190
And as always as you're watching,

00:00:38.190 --> 00:00:40.566
if you hear something that
really resonates with you,

00:00:40.566 --> 00:00:42.270
please leave it in the comments below.

00:00:42.270 --> 00:00:43.103
Put quotes around it

00:00:43.103 --> 00:00:45.061
so other people can be inspired as well.

00:00:45.061 --> 00:00:46.229
And when you write it down,

00:00:46.229 --> 00:00:48.751
it's much more likely to
stick with you as well.

00:00:48.751 --> 00:00:49.584
Enjoy.

00:00:53.501 --> 00:00:56.084
(upbeat music)

00:01:03.015 --> 00:01:04.868
- So then I go to the Essence Awards

00:01:04.868 --> 00:01:08.104
the day after the event that you had.

00:01:08.104 --> 00:01:12.697
We've all been to the
Essence Awards and you spoke

00:01:12.697 --> 00:01:15.030
and as you started to speak,

00:01:15.971 --> 00:01:20.003
you were getting the
Fierce and Fearless Award.

00:01:20.003 --> 00:01:22.584
Obviously, you had given
that a lot of thought.

00:01:22.584 --> 00:01:24.539
And as you started to speak,

00:01:24.539 --> 00:01:27.528
my own mouth dropped and
then it got wider and wider.

00:01:27.528 --> 00:01:29.256
By the time you finished we were all like,

00:01:29.256 --> 00:01:30.923
whoa, what was that?

00:01:32.113 --> 00:01:34.363
(applause)

00:01:36.559 --> 00:01:40.226
- We live in a town
that rewards pretending.

00:01:42.747 --> 00:01:45.486
And I had been pretending

00:01:45.486 --> 00:01:49.403
to be fierce and fearless
for a very long time.

00:01:50.792 --> 00:01:54.292
I was a victim masquerading as a survivor.

00:01:56.751 --> 00:02:00.418
I used to revel in
gossip and rumors and the

00:02:04.451 --> 00:02:08.333
and I lived for the negativity inflicted

00:02:08.333 --> 00:02:11.734
upon my sister actresses or anyone

00:02:11.734 --> 00:02:15.151
who I felt whose shine diminished my own.

00:02:17.297 --> 00:02:18.455
Fortunate enough to be honored

00:02:18.455 --> 00:02:20.263
at the Essence Awards Luncheon

00:02:20.263 --> 00:02:21.535
for the Fierce and Fearless Award.

00:02:21.535 --> 00:02:22.973
I was talking to my girlfriend,

00:02:22.973 --> 00:02:24.991
A.J. Johnson who's my trainer

00:02:24.991 --> 00:02:27.580
but she's also like a life coach,

00:02:27.580 --> 00:02:29.536
and I was like, do I tell it?

00:02:29.536 --> 00:02:30.474
I mean if I'm getting an award

00:02:30.474 --> 00:02:31.932
for being Fierce and Fearless,

00:02:31.932 --> 00:02:33.677
how about if I really
be fierce and fearless

00:02:33.677 --> 00:02:37.238
and explain to people my evolution.

00:02:37.238 --> 00:02:39.071
I love who I am today,

00:02:39.071 --> 00:02:40.407
but that wasn't always the case.

00:02:40.407 --> 00:02:42.400
I didn't love my features.

00:02:42.400 --> 00:02:43.539
I didn't love my weight.

00:02:43.539 --> 00:02:44.404
I didn't my hair.

00:02:44.404 --> 00:02:46.105
I didn't love my lips.

00:02:46.105 --> 00:02:47.122
And it's been an evolution

00:02:47.122 --> 00:02:49.229
and I wasn't always nice

00:02:49.229 --> 00:02:51.583
or as gracious as I could have been

00:02:51.583 --> 00:02:53.061
or happy for other people.

00:02:53.061 --> 00:02:54.471
And just sort of explain that journey

00:02:54.471 --> 00:02:56.508
through my speech.

00:02:56.508 --> 00:02:59.558
It had been such a long
journey to get to that point.

00:02:59.558 --> 00:03:02.725
And I started doing the work on myself

00:03:04.364 --> 00:03:06.338
and really wanting to be the woman

00:03:06.338 --> 00:03:09.548
I always sort of dreamed I wanted to be,

00:03:09.548 --> 00:03:12.293
but when I got divorced and
I had a career set-back,

00:03:12.293 --> 00:03:14.026
I had hit basically, rock-bottom.

00:03:14.026 --> 00:03:15.380
I had reached out to A.J. Johnson

00:03:15.380 --> 00:03:17.775
and we started doing the work,

00:03:17.775 --> 00:03:20.110
and being honest and
really, really looking

00:03:20.110 --> 00:03:22.785
at myself and my life, and my choices.

00:03:22.785 --> 00:03:24.266
- So A.J. Johnson was a coach?

00:03:24.266 --> 00:03:25.949
- [Gabrielle] Is my, yeah like
she was a physical trainer

00:03:25.949 --> 00:03:28.014
but also like a life coach.

00:03:28.014 --> 00:03:31.126
And she was like let's really, you ready?

00:03:31.126 --> 00:03:31.959
I don't think you're ready.

00:03:31.959 --> 00:03:32.792
I don't really think you're ready

00:03:32.792 --> 00:03:34.438
to really look at your
life and your choices,

00:03:34.438 --> 00:03:36.216
I think you like how you live.

00:03:36.216 --> 00:03:37.059
I think you think it's cute.

00:03:37.059 --> 00:03:39.220
I think you think, I
make a living doing this,

00:03:39.220 --> 00:03:40.350
I make a lot of money doing this

00:03:40.350 --> 00:03:41.852
so why should I change.

00:03:41.852 --> 00:03:43.602
And I was like, true.

00:03:44.607 --> 00:03:48.043
So I had to really examine
all the choices I've made

00:03:48.043 --> 00:03:51.478
as an adult and what I
like and what I don't like,

00:03:51.478 --> 00:03:53.586
and there was a lot I didn't like.

00:03:53.586 --> 00:03:56.516
So from that point on
in like my early 30's,

00:03:56.516 --> 00:03:59.117
I started really living my truth

00:03:59.117 --> 00:04:01.228
and my words matched my actions.

00:04:01.228 --> 00:04:03.044
So when I was putting together a speech

00:04:03.044 --> 00:04:04.112
about Fierce and Fearless,

00:04:04.112 --> 00:04:06.482
I was like, A.J. do I tell it?

00:04:06.482 --> 00:04:10.268
Do I really tell people
what this journey has been?

00:04:10.268 --> 00:04:11.984
Because you know people,
they see you on a red carpet

00:04:11.984 --> 00:04:13.959
or they see you in a
picture or in an interview,

00:04:13.959 --> 00:04:18.445
and they're like, oh she must
be extra perfect or whatever.

00:04:18.445 --> 00:04:20.487
- People have their
perceptions of what they think

00:04:20.487 --> 00:04:21.960
your life is like.

00:04:21.960 --> 00:04:22.793
- Absolutely.

00:04:22.793 --> 00:04:26.313
- And it's been the absolute opposite.

00:04:26.313 --> 00:04:27.480
Going through,

00:04:27.480 --> 00:04:31.647
going from sexual assault
victim to rape survivor,

00:04:32.512 --> 00:04:33.450
going through a divorce,

00:04:33.450 --> 00:04:34.955
having career set-backs,

00:04:34.955 --> 00:04:37.555
re-examining why you even
are in this business.

00:04:37.555 --> 00:04:38.388
Who am I?

00:04:38.388 --> 00:04:40.706
Who do I want to be to the world?

00:04:40.706 --> 00:04:41.964
That's what we were like,

00:04:41.964 --> 00:04:42.960
let's just tell it.
- Yeah.

00:04:42.960 --> 00:04:44.169
Let the chips fall where they may!

00:04:44.169 --> 00:04:45.936
And I never thought that being honest

00:04:45.936 --> 00:04:47.958
would have that kind of reaction.

00:04:47.958 --> 00:04:49.804
- Gab, I know you had some
issues when coming back

00:04:49.804 --> 00:04:52.517
for this new season of Being Mary Jane.

00:04:52.517 --> 00:04:53.838
And as a woman, as an actress,

00:04:53.838 --> 00:04:55.838
as a director, can we
talk about equal pay?

00:04:55.838 --> 00:04:57.286
'Cause I know it something
to do with equal pay.

00:04:57.286 --> 00:04:58.576
I don't know the details

00:04:58.576 --> 00:05:00.140
when it came to your battle with BET,

00:05:00.140 --> 00:05:01.215
and everything that happened.

00:05:01.215 --> 00:05:03.377
- Well it actually didn't
which was interesting that,

00:05:03.377 --> 00:05:06.460
but I'm happy to tackle gender equity

00:05:07.575 --> 00:05:10.627
when it comes to my financial statements.

00:05:10.627 --> 00:05:14.195
We're doing the same amount of work

00:05:14.195 --> 00:05:18.611
and if my star and your
star is in the same place,

00:05:18.611 --> 00:05:19.981
and I bring to the table
the exact same thing

00:05:19.981 --> 00:05:23.063
you bring to the table, we
should be paid the exact same.

00:05:23.063 --> 00:05:25.385
It's not like I'm only
on a couple episodes

00:05:25.385 --> 00:05:26.856
or I'm only working 15 minutes

00:05:26.856 --> 00:05:28.360
and you're there everyday all day,

00:05:28.360 --> 00:05:30.281
that's something different.

00:05:30.281 --> 00:05:31.902
But if we're doing the same job

00:05:31.902 --> 00:05:33.323
and we're bringing the
same thing to the table,

00:05:33.323 --> 00:05:34.170
give me my money,

00:05:34.170 --> 00:05:36.040
give me the same thing
that you're giving him.

00:05:36.040 --> 00:05:39.343
I will go, I would rather
use all of my money

00:05:39.343 --> 00:05:42.647
towards lawsuits for pay equity.

00:05:42.647 --> 00:05:43.644
But at the end of the day,

00:05:43.644 --> 00:05:44.844
if you don't stand up for something,

00:05:44.844 --> 00:05:45.813
in this industry,

00:05:45.813 --> 00:05:46.982
you will fall for everything

00:05:46.982 --> 00:05:49.208
and you will not be
compensated on the way down.

00:05:49.208 --> 00:05:51.708
So that is my overall message.

00:05:53.264 --> 00:05:57.431
If there's something that
you find that is unequitable,

00:05:58.333 --> 00:06:00.530
unfair, it's up to you.

00:06:00.530 --> 00:06:01.864
No one's going to fight your battles.

00:06:01.864 --> 00:06:02.697
If they can save money

00:06:02.697 --> 00:06:04.030
not paying you--
- Oh, they will.

00:06:04.030 --> 00:06:04.863
they will.

00:06:04.863 --> 00:06:07.667
So you have to be your biggest,

00:06:07.667 --> 00:06:09.433
your own biggest and best advocate.

00:06:09.433 --> 00:06:12.520
- But speaking of fighting
for what you believe is right,

00:06:12.520 --> 00:06:14.150
how many times, coming up in your career,

00:06:14.150 --> 00:06:15.020
did it backfire on you?

00:06:15.020 --> 00:06:16.299
Did you decide to put your foot down?

00:06:16.299 --> 00:06:19.863
And they'll be like all
right, then we don't need you.

00:06:19.863 --> 00:06:20.696
- Never.

00:06:21.608 --> 00:06:22.736
- 'Cause I sometimes believe
that a lot of women get scared.

00:06:22.736 --> 00:06:26.729
You know what I mean?
- A lot of us get scared.

00:06:26.729 --> 00:06:27.811
- There were times I just didn't do it

00:06:27.811 --> 00:06:29.773
so that's different then doing it

00:06:29.773 --> 00:06:32.068
and it blowing up in my face.

00:06:32.068 --> 00:06:35.652
Never ever have I opened
my mouth to speak out

00:06:35.652 --> 00:06:38.247
against some kind of injustice at work

00:06:38.247 --> 00:06:39.478
whether that be something sexist,

00:06:39.478 --> 00:06:41.463
something racist, something misogynistic,

00:06:41.463 --> 00:06:45.298
something just flat-out wack or unfair

00:06:45.298 --> 00:06:46.984
where it ever came back negatively,

00:06:46.984 --> 00:06:48.487
and affected my opportunities.

00:06:48.487 --> 00:06:51.191
If anything, people
have more respect for me

00:06:51.191 --> 00:06:52.893
and like having me around

00:06:52.893 --> 00:06:55.780
'cause they'd rather me speak
up than them half the time.

00:06:55.780 --> 00:06:58.234
I don't ever shy away from that.

00:06:58.234 --> 00:06:59.671
- How do you deal with feedback?

00:06:59.671 --> 00:07:00.504
Criticism?

00:07:00.504 --> 00:07:02.131
Positive or negative?

00:07:02.131 --> 00:07:03.453
- You take it all with a grain of salt.

00:07:03.453 --> 00:07:06.229
I mean early in my career,

00:07:06.229 --> 00:07:08.646
I was named the next It girl,

00:07:09.582 --> 00:07:10.469
and you're like,

00:07:10.469 --> 00:07:13.990
well I think I should really believe this.

00:07:13.990 --> 00:07:17.340
And then you read, you're
the worst thing ever,

00:07:17.340 --> 00:07:18.763
you should never leave the house.

00:07:18.763 --> 00:07:20.614
And you're like, oh we
should throw that out.

00:07:20.614 --> 00:07:22.556
Eventually, you just
kind of get to a place

00:07:22.556 --> 00:07:24.423
where they kind of cancel each other out.

00:07:24.423 --> 00:07:25.609
You're going to hear the naysayers

00:07:25.609 --> 00:07:26.764
and the people who think you suck

00:07:26.764 --> 00:07:28.010
and then there are going to be the people

00:07:28.010 --> 00:07:30.994
who think you're the
Second Coming of Pockets.

00:07:30.994 --> 00:07:32.685
It's usually somewhere in the middle.

00:07:32.685 --> 00:07:34.069
(audience laughs)

00:07:34.069 --> 00:07:37.018
If you believe all your praise,

00:07:37.018 --> 00:07:38.968
there's no where to go,
you're not going to grow.

00:07:38.968 --> 00:07:41.966
And if you believe every
negative thing about you,

00:07:41.966 --> 00:07:44.044
you're not going to get out of bed.

00:07:44.044 --> 00:07:45.963
So I try to be reasonable,

00:07:45.963 --> 00:07:49.733
people whose opinion I respect, I listen.

00:07:49.733 --> 00:07:51.016
Like when Regina King,

00:07:51.016 --> 00:07:54.590
she directs four episodes
this season of Being Mary Jane

00:07:54.590 --> 00:07:55.712
and she's a good friend,

00:07:55.712 --> 00:07:57.962
but she never let me slide.

00:07:58.927 --> 00:08:00.825
We shoot a lot, we shoot
almost 10 pages a day

00:08:00.825 --> 00:08:04.360
which is sort of unheard of in television.

00:08:04.360 --> 00:08:07.248
You can get a little lazy, to be honest.

00:08:07.248 --> 00:08:08.765
And she would never let me be lazy,

00:08:08.765 --> 00:08:10.109
she'll be like, G?

00:08:10.109 --> 00:08:11.884
Come on now, come on now.

00:08:11.884 --> 00:08:13.338
(growls)

00:08:13.338 --> 00:08:17.123
So it's nice to have people
who will call you on your shit,

00:08:17.123 --> 00:08:18.645
and can we say shit on?

00:08:18.645 --> 00:08:19.954
It's the internet.

00:08:19.954 --> 00:08:22.311
- We're grownups, come on.

00:08:22.311 --> 00:08:23.716
- Well if my lip can be
sweaty, I can say shit.

00:08:23.716 --> 00:08:26.684
Who will call you on your shit

00:08:26.684 --> 00:08:30.277
and make you accountable
and make you better.

00:08:30.277 --> 00:08:32.352
And that's huge.

00:08:32.352 --> 00:08:34.487
If I could leave you with anything,

00:08:34.487 --> 00:08:36.925
is you have to value yourself.

00:08:36.925 --> 00:08:39.317
And it sounds so super
cliche and everybody says it,

00:08:39.317 --> 00:08:40.516
and if you don't value yourself,

00:08:40.516 --> 00:08:41.349
you don't love yourself,

00:08:41.349 --> 00:08:42.182
no one's going to love you.

00:08:42.182 --> 00:08:45.432
But seriously, I just realized that at,

00:08:46.566 --> 00:08:48.919
I got divorced, my show got canceled.

00:08:48.919 --> 00:08:52.963
Had all these terrible things
happen and I hit rock-bottom.

00:08:52.963 --> 00:08:56.630
What I realized is I'm
an educated, amazing,

00:08:57.536 --> 00:08:59.619
vibrant, relevant person.

00:09:01.714 --> 00:09:04.964
One bad thing does not define who I am.

00:09:06.152 --> 00:09:08.424
I am so much more than a failed TV show

00:09:08.424 --> 00:09:09.433
or a failed marriage

00:09:09.433 --> 00:09:10.702
or what the blogs say,

00:09:10.702 --> 00:09:12.586
I'm so much more than that.

00:09:12.586 --> 00:09:15.115
- Most significant skill set

00:09:15.115 --> 00:09:17.866
or characteristic you
developed as an athlete

00:09:17.866 --> 00:09:20.500
that has enabled you to be
successful in your career?

00:09:20.500 --> 00:09:23.262
- Leadership, absolutely.

00:09:23.262 --> 00:09:25.862
There's something about
being able to direct

00:09:25.862 --> 00:09:27.326
the action on the court

00:09:27.326 --> 00:09:30.098
that informs your personality.

00:09:30.098 --> 00:09:32.617
I took away different skills

00:09:32.617 --> 00:09:35.766
just from working with the group of women,

00:09:35.766 --> 00:09:37.798
leading a group of women,

00:09:37.798 --> 00:09:41.542
trying to form an identity for our team.

00:09:41.542 --> 00:09:44.038
And that identity, above everything else,

00:09:44.038 --> 00:09:45.165
was be your own leader,

00:09:45.165 --> 00:09:47.686
resilience and stick together.

00:09:47.686 --> 00:09:48.870
- [Interviewer] And what my platform is

00:09:48.870 --> 00:09:49.882
learning to love yourself.

00:09:49.882 --> 00:09:51.571
So could you tell me a little
bit about any insecurities

00:09:51.571 --> 00:09:54.068
you may have had and how you
learned to overcome them?

00:09:54.068 --> 00:09:56.009
- I think I can tell you
insecurities I didn't have.

00:09:56.009 --> 00:09:56.926
Everything.

00:09:57.864 --> 00:10:00.365
I mean growing up as the
darkest girl in my family,

00:10:00.365 --> 00:10:02.508
growing up super thin,

00:10:02.508 --> 00:10:06.619
not having secondary
sexual characteristics

00:10:06.619 --> 00:10:08.710
come in until much later,

00:10:08.710 --> 00:10:12.080
being the only black girl
in all-white communities.

00:10:12.080 --> 00:10:14.257
I could go on and on, and on.

00:10:14.257 --> 00:10:16.576
Like literally feeling like I shrink

00:10:16.576 --> 00:10:18.529
when a beautiful woman walks in.

00:10:18.529 --> 00:10:19.529
All of that.

00:10:20.616 --> 00:10:22.283
It's been a journey.

00:10:23.510 --> 00:10:27.375
You have to make a
commitment to wanting better

00:10:27.375 --> 00:10:28.749
than functioning in dysfunction.

00:10:28.749 --> 00:10:32.901
I'm those black people
that you meet in life

00:10:32.901 --> 00:10:33.958
where if someone says,

00:10:33.958 --> 00:10:35.763
I'm not a racist, I've got a black friend,

00:10:35.763 --> 00:10:37.950
I would've been that black friend.

00:10:37.950 --> 00:10:39.925
(audience laughs)

00:10:39.925 --> 00:10:42.092
Assimilation was complete.

00:10:43.997 --> 00:10:46.790
Along with being the chip in the cookie

00:10:46.790 --> 00:10:48.488
at a very young age,

00:10:48.488 --> 00:10:50.850
came the advice from my parents,

00:10:50.850 --> 00:10:51.683
which I think a lot of our parents

00:10:51.683 --> 00:10:53.309
in this room have probably given us,

00:10:53.309 --> 00:10:55.097
you are going to have to
be bigger, badder, better

00:10:55.097 --> 00:10:56.925
just to be considered equal.

00:10:56.925 --> 00:10:59.884
(audience cheers and applauds)

00:10:59.884 --> 00:11:01.672
Which is very accurate.

00:11:01.672 --> 00:11:06.277
But what it does to the
self-esteem of a small child

00:11:06.277 --> 00:11:07.750
is to say that,

00:11:07.750 --> 00:11:11.842
you are always going
to not be good enough.

00:11:11.842 --> 00:11:15.349
So in school, I would
try to do this to my lips

00:11:15.349 --> 00:11:17.383
so I wouldn't have big lips,

00:11:17.383 --> 00:11:19.098
didn't want to be too black,

00:11:19.098 --> 00:11:21.555
had to make sure that I always got those,

00:11:21.555 --> 00:11:23.353
you're so articulate compliments,

00:11:23.353 --> 00:11:24.759
which by the way,

00:11:24.759 --> 00:11:26.148
if you ever say that to an adult,

00:11:26.148 --> 00:11:28.229
it's actually not a compliment.

00:11:28.229 --> 00:11:31.229
(audience chuckles)

00:11:32.226 --> 00:11:36.059
I wanted to make sure
my hair was so straight.

00:11:37.176 --> 00:11:39.645
I used to leave relaxers
on my hair so long,

00:11:39.645 --> 00:11:42.870
I would get lesions
because I wanted to fit in.

00:11:42.870 --> 00:11:43.924
I wanted to be good enough.

00:11:43.924 --> 00:11:45.034
I didn't want to be a joke.

00:11:45.034 --> 00:11:47.327
I didn't want to be a loser.

00:11:47.327 --> 00:11:50.125
Anytime some guy did not return my love,

00:11:50.125 --> 00:11:52.397
it was because I'm not good enough

00:11:52.397 --> 00:11:54.114
because I'm a joke, I'm a loser.

00:11:54.114 --> 00:11:57.947
When I got raped at 19
at my after-school job,

00:11:59.073 --> 00:12:02.240
it wasn't just some awful coincidence,

00:12:04.105 --> 00:12:06.522
some terrible freak accident.

00:12:09.188 --> 00:12:11.161
It wasn't an unspeakable crime,

00:12:11.161 --> 00:12:13.281
it was because I was a joke and a loser,

00:12:13.281 --> 00:12:15.364
and this is what happens.

00:12:16.567 --> 00:12:18.234
When I got divorced,

00:12:20.271 --> 00:12:22.451
I'm a joke and a loser, of course.

00:12:22.451 --> 00:12:26.368
Show gets canceled, joke
and a loser of course.

00:12:29.226 --> 00:12:31.393
And on that day in August,

00:12:32.602 --> 00:12:34.692
when I started doing the work,

00:12:34.692 --> 00:12:38.371
they were like, you got to replace that

00:12:38.371 --> 00:12:39.556
that voice in your head

00:12:39.556 --> 00:12:41.963
that's telling you you're
a joke and a loser.

00:12:41.963 --> 00:12:44.382
You got to stop being crippled by a fear

00:12:44.382 --> 00:12:46.382
of possible humiliation.

00:12:47.792 --> 00:12:49.573
That little voice that pops
up in your head that says,

00:12:49.573 --> 00:12:50.406
don't raise your hand,

00:12:50.406 --> 00:12:52.242
you're not going to
answer the question right.

00:12:52.242 --> 00:12:54.065
Don't put that on, you're too big.

00:12:54.065 --> 00:12:57.107
Don't wear your hair
like that, it's so ugly.

00:12:57.107 --> 00:12:59.316
Nothing in my closet works.

00:12:59.316 --> 00:13:01.864
I'm so dumb, I can't do it.

00:13:01.864 --> 00:13:03.473
No one's going to love me.

00:13:03.473 --> 00:13:05.140
Why is my pain meek?

00:13:06.377 --> 00:13:07.460
Replace that.

00:13:09.398 --> 00:13:12.481
And it sounded so cliche and so easy.

00:13:18.123 --> 00:13:21.540
That day I decided to stop telling myself

00:13:22.775 --> 00:13:25.025
that I was a joke and a loser,

00:13:25.025 --> 00:13:27.437
that I was dope and fly, and the reason...

00:13:27.437 --> 00:13:30.622
What sports taught me is
how to work within a group

00:13:30.622 --> 00:13:33.539
and how to find strength in a team.

00:13:34.599 --> 00:13:36.601
Same with after-school activities,

00:13:36.601 --> 00:13:39.164
I was in the Spanish club.

00:13:39.164 --> 00:13:40.097
(laughs)

00:13:40.097 --> 00:13:41.347
(speaking Spanish)

00:13:41.347 --> 00:13:43.312
(laughs)

00:13:43.312 --> 00:13:44.254
- [Man] Oh really?

00:13:44.254 --> 00:13:46.909
(audience laughs)

00:13:46.909 --> 00:13:48.553
- It had helped to have
strength in numbers

00:13:48.553 --> 00:13:50.986
and know how to function within a group

00:13:50.986 --> 00:13:53.309
because in life, you're not an island.

00:13:53.309 --> 00:13:54.596
You're not by yourself

00:13:54.596 --> 00:13:56.206
even though sometimes it feels like it,

00:13:56.206 --> 00:13:58.691
you need to know how
to work within a group

00:13:58.691 --> 00:14:02.418
and how to pull different
your positive attributes,

00:14:02.418 --> 00:14:03.608
your positive attributes,

00:14:03.608 --> 00:14:05.752
so we can be a strong unit.

00:14:05.752 --> 00:14:09.034
But when you are looking to
find other people in life

00:14:09.034 --> 00:14:10.606
that will help you be successful

00:14:10.606 --> 00:14:12.525
and keep you on the right path,

00:14:12.525 --> 00:14:15.423
it's that team mentality of,

00:14:15.423 --> 00:14:17.690
okay you're better at this than I am,

00:14:17.690 --> 00:14:18.815
you're better at,

00:14:18.815 --> 00:14:22.112
you know my girl Dawn,
she's a marketing guru,

00:14:22.112 --> 00:14:24.863
so we all go to Dawn when we need help

00:14:24.863 --> 00:14:26.778
in terms of how best to market ourselves

00:14:26.778 --> 00:14:28.228
'cause a lot of us are unemployed.

00:14:28.228 --> 00:14:30.736
A lot of my friends lost their jobs

00:14:30.736 --> 00:14:34.903
so we're like how do we to
Dawn to help her, help us?

00:14:36.208 --> 00:14:38.542
Utilizing her skills that can enable us

00:14:38.542 --> 00:14:40.590
to become better people.

00:14:40.590 --> 00:14:42.031
I live for the quiet moments

00:14:42.031 --> 00:14:44.648
where I can be my most authentic self

00:14:44.648 --> 00:14:46.347
and hear myself think.

00:14:46.347 --> 00:14:48.488
Somebody asked me, what makes you happy?

00:14:48.488 --> 00:14:50.462
My husband said, bacon.

00:14:50.462 --> 00:14:51.881
(audience laughs)

00:14:51.881 --> 00:14:53.048
Which is true.

00:14:54.276 --> 00:14:58.443
But I'm happiest when I'm
at my most authentic self.

00:14:59.837 --> 00:15:02.711
When nobody's looking,
when nobody's judging me,

00:15:02.711 --> 00:15:07.610
when nobody's leaving nasty
comments on my social media.

00:15:07.610 --> 00:15:10.170
And I can just exist.

00:15:10.170 --> 00:15:13.003
And in that quiet space I realized

00:15:13.907 --> 00:15:16.074
I am worthy by birthright.

00:15:18.559 --> 00:15:22.142
I am fierce and fabulous
because I breathe.

00:15:23.157 --> 00:15:25.490
All of us here in this room,

00:15:26.889 --> 00:15:29.222
we are worthy, we are valid.

00:15:30.378 --> 00:15:33.461
Our journeys are real and worthwhile.

00:15:36.566 --> 00:15:39.010
And there's nothing that anyone can do

00:15:39.010 --> 00:15:40.076
to take that away from us.

00:15:40.076 --> 00:15:42.484
Everything terrible
that has happened to us,

00:15:42.484 --> 00:15:45.019
we have a choice in how we ought to react.

00:15:45.019 --> 00:15:47.854
A lot of times what we're
actually reacting to,

00:15:47.854 --> 00:15:50.104
is the fear of humiliation,

00:15:51.406 --> 00:15:54.395
the fear of, what are they
going to think about me?

00:15:54.395 --> 00:15:56.420
The fear of possible judgment.

00:15:56.420 --> 00:15:58.512
Newsflash, people will judge you

00:15:58.512 --> 00:16:00.534
whether you discovered the cure for cancer

00:16:00.534 --> 00:16:02.201
or sit on the couch.

00:16:03.663 --> 00:16:05.580
You might as well live.

00:16:07.639 --> 00:16:08.556
I am a wife

00:16:10.679 --> 00:16:13.012
but that does not define me.

00:16:14.564 --> 00:16:19.232
I'm an actress and that sure
as hell, does not define me.

00:16:19.232 --> 00:16:21.482
I'm a parent while awesome,

00:16:22.959 --> 00:16:25.126
that is not my whole life.

00:16:26.390 --> 00:16:27.953
None of those things

00:16:27.953 --> 00:16:32.120
even though I get a lot of
praise for that, makes me worthy.

00:16:33.252 --> 00:16:35.419
I am worthy by birthright.

00:16:36.385 --> 00:16:39.254
I am Gabrielle Union-Wade.

00:16:39.254 --> 00:16:41.040
(audience applauds)

00:16:41.040 --> 00:16:43.225
(school bell rings)

00:16:43.225 --> 00:16:44.086
(chuckles)

00:16:44.086 --> 00:16:45.637
